## Key Discussion Points

### Administration & Side Meeting Report
* **Chairs:** Mališa Vučinić, Francesc-Xavier Aguiló
* **Slides:** [00-Chairs' slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lake-00-chairs-slides-01)
* **Document Status:**
  * `draft-ietf-lake-private-use-ranges` was recently adopted by the working group.
  * `draft-ietf-lake-edhoc-psk` completed shepherd review and is ready for submission to the IESG.
  * `draft-ietf-lake-authz` completed Working Group Last Call (WGLC).
* **Side Meeting Summary (Nov 18, 2026):**
  * Discussed extension compatibility issues across RFC 9528 message flows and new authentication methods (e.g., assumptions in EAD extensions about responder authentication in Message 2).
  * Decided to form a design team to analyze security properties required by extensions rather than relying on fixed message sequence numbers.
  * Discussed post-quantum transition for Methods 1 and 3: a liaison/request was sent to CFRG (2026-09-13) requesting standardization of a lightweight Non-Interactive Key Exchange (NIKE). Once available, LAKE can register corresponding cipher suites. In the interim, KEM-based authentication methods (`draft-ietf-lake-authkem-edhoc`) provide post-quantum capability.

