### Remote Attestation over LAKE (`draft-ietf-lake-ra`)
* **Presenter:** Yushun Li
* **Slides:** [03-Remote Attestation over LAKE](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lake-03-remote-attestation-over-lake-01)
* **Discussion:**
  * Restructured Section 5 to consolidate EAD items for Background Check and Passport models under two EAD labels.
  * Updated privacy considerations: personally identifiable information (PII) carried in evidence must be protected against active/passive attackers, meaning evidence must not be sent before Message 3 (for Methods 0–3) or Message 4 (for PSK).
  * Planned future integration with additional post-handshake messages ($Message_n$) to allow more flexible evidence transmission.
  * Usama Mansoor asked about active attackers acting as initiators; Mališa Vučinić and Yushun Li clarified that evidence is only disclosed after mutual authentication is established.

