### KEM-based Authentication for EDHOC (`draft-ietf-lake-authkem-edhoc`)
* **Presenter:** Lydia de la Torre
* **Slides:** [04-draft-ietf-lake-authkem-edhoc-01](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lake-04-draft-ietf-lake-authkem-edhoc-01-01)
* **Discussion:**
  * Draft -01 removed duplicate cipher suite registrations, delegating algorithm definitions to `draft-ietf-lake-pqsuites`.
  * Key schedule updated to use `TH5` and `KEY5` for protecting Message 5. Proposed KDF labels 13 and 14 for harmonization.
  * Preserved AEAD protection in Message 3 to prevent identity disclosure attacks via unauthenticated payload manipulation.
  * Authors favor requiring the same KEM algorithm for both key exchange and authentication to minimize memory footprint in constrained devices.
  * Discussed whether Message 5 (MAC3) could be optional or replaced by protected application data if key confirmation is implicitly guaranteed; formal verification will evaluate this option.

