### Quantum-Resistant Cipher Suites for LAKE (`draft-ietf-lake-pqsuites`) & Hybridization
* **Presenter:** Clement Papon
* **Slides:** [05-draft-ietf-lake-pqsuites](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lake-05-draft-ietf-lake-pqsuites-00)
* **Discussion:**
  * Defines PQ cipher suites combining ML-KEM (ephemeral key exchange) and ML-DSA (signatures) for Method 0 and PSK.
  * Uses SHAKE256 for LAKE hash and SHA-256 for application hash.
  * Restructured security considerations to address store-now-decrypt-later attacks and side-channel protections. Renamed IANA registry prefixes from `EDHOC` to `LAKE`.
  * **Hybridization Discussion:** Discussed whether to support hybrid post-quantum/classical schemes. John Preuß Mattsson, Francesc-Xavier Aguiló, and Clement Papon agreed that hybrid algorithms should be defined at the algorithm level (via CFRG/COSE) in a separate document to prevent delaying `draft-ietf-lake-pqsuites`.

