### Formal Verification of KEM-based Authentication for LAKE
* **Presenter:** Vaishnavi Sundararajan
* **Slides:** [09-Formal verification of KEM-based authentication for LAKE](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lake-09-formal-verification-of-kem-based-authentication-for-edhoc-02)
* **Discussion:**
  * Formally analyzed KEM-based authentication (`draft-ietf-lake-authkem-edhoc-01`) using ProVerif in the Dolev-Yao model with store-now-decrypt-later extensions.
  * Confirmed mutual authentication, injective agreement on key material/identifiers, perfect forward secrecy (even under ephemeral or long-term key compromise), and identity anonymity for initiator and responder.
  * Verified that protocol design inherently prevents re-encapsulation attacks.
  * Future work includes modeling trustworthiness checks, porting to Tamarind/SAPIK+, and testing the impact of omitting Message 5 MAC3.

