### AFS-KEX Protocol with Lattice/Isogeny Instantiations
* **Presenter:** Junlei Lin
* **Slides:** [10-AFS-KEX Protocol with Concrete Lattice/Isogeny Instantiations Based on ML-KEM and MIKE](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lake-11-afs-kex-protocol-with-concrete-latticeisogeny-instantiations-based-on-ml-kem-and-mike-00)
* **Discussion:**
  * Presented AFS-KEX (ML-KEM based) and AFS-MIKE (Isogeny based) post-quantum key exchange protocols.
  * AFS-KEX offers 3- or 4-round execution, identity hiding in the CRS model, and resilience to exposure of 3 out of 4 secret keys.
  * AFS-MIKE achieves signature-free 3-round authenticated key exchange with identity hiding.
  * Lydia de la Torre noted that size comparison with KEM-based EDHOC must consider credential reference optimizations already supported in LAKE. Scott Fluhrer noted the high computational complexity of isogeny operations.

